# tron plugin — environment variables
#
# The Confluence / ImageKit / content skills read these from the shell environment.
# On the reference setup they live in ~/.env (generated by 1Password) and are
# auto-sourced; the bundled fetch-confluence.sh also sources ~/.env on demand if a
# token is missing. Copy the keys you need into your own ~/.env (or export them in
# your shell, or add them to your marketing-pages .env.local), then fill in real
# values. NEVER commit real secrets — this file is the template, not the secret store.
#
# Tools that authenticate on their own (acli, gh, codex) are NOT listed here — log
# into those separately (`acli jira auth`, `gh auth login`, `codex login`).

# --- Atlassian (Jira + Confluence) ---

# Your Atlassian account email. Used for Confluence REST basic auth in the
# image-attachment download path (tron:news-item, tron:guide-item). If unset, the
# fetch script falls back to `git config user.email`.
ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=you@facilitron.com

# Atlassian API token — create at:
#   https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
# Used by tron:confluence, tron:news-item, tron:guide-item for REST fetches/downloads.
JIRA_API_TOKEN=

# --- ImageKit CDN ---

# Private key for the Facilitron ImageKit account (ImageKit dashboard → Developer
# Options → API Keys). Required by every skill that uploads media: tron:news-item,
# tron:toolkit-item, tron:guide-item, tron:figma-to-imagekit, tron:md-to-pdf.
IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY=
